185 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (One critical question arises amidst this sprawl: Where do your metric definitions live? If they are trapped in a dashboard created in Tableau, how can analysts who prefer Power BI inherit those definitions? When business logic is tied to individual tools, consistent metrics become nearly impossible to manage, leading to disconnected reporting, frustrated users, and wasted effort.)
/E (One critical question arises amidst this sprawl: Where do your metric definitions live? If they are trapped in a dashboard created in Tableau, how can analysts who prefer Power BI inherit those definitions? When business logic is tied to individual tools, consistent metrics become nearly impossible to manage, leading to disconnected reporting, frustrated users, and wasted effort.)
/Pg 10 0 R
>>
endobj
186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The consequences of this fragmentation are hitting your bottom line and hampering your decision-making capabilities. You're paying for overlapping licenses while your teams debate whose numbers are correct. Your IT staff stretches thin, maintaining expertise across numerous platforms, and your security team struggles to ensure consistent controls across disconnected systems. Most critically, your business leaders lose trust in analytics when different tools produce conflicting answers to the same question.)
/E (The consequences of this fragmentation are hitting your bottom line and hampering your decision-making capabilities. You're paying for overlapping licenses while your teams debate whose numbers are correct. Your IT staff stretches thin, maintaining expertise across numerous platforms, and your security team struggles to ensure consistent controls across disconnected systems. Most critically, your business leaders lose trust in analytics when different tools produce conflicting answers to the same question.)
/Pg 10 0 R
>>
endobj
