/S /H2
/T (If you're like most organizations, your BI landscape has grown organically over the years. Perhaps your marketing department selected one visualization tool while finance standardized on another. Maybe you've acquired companies that brought their own analytics platforms, or your teams have implemented proofs-of-concepts that quietly became production systems.)
/E (If you're like most organizations, your BI landscape has grown organically over the years. Perhaps your marketing department selected one visualization tool while finance standardized on another. Maybe you've acquired companies that brought their own analytics platforms, or your teams have implemented proofs-of-concepts that quietly became production systems.)
/Pg 10 0 R
>>
