/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (1. Universal Semantic Layer)
/E (1. Universal Semantic Layer)
/Pg 14 0 R
>>
endobj
300 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (At the core of Strategy's recommended approach is a universal semantic layer that serves as the single source of truth for business definitions, metrics, and data access. This critical component translates complex technical data structures into intuitive, business-friendly objects that users can understand and trust, regardless of their preferred visualization tool.)
/E (At the core of Strategy's recommended approach is a universal semantic layer that serves as the single source of truth for business definitions, metrics, and data access. This critical component translates complex technical data structures into intuitive, business-friendly objects that users can understand and trust, regardless of their preferred visualization tool.)
/Pg 14 0 R
>>
endobj
301 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (What sets the Universal Semantic Layer apart is its unique ability to support agentic AI systems that act autonomously and make informed decisions based on governed, consistent, and reusable metrics. By building a foundation of rich semantics, this layer not only feeds agents clean and reliable data but also equips them with contextual business logic, dynamic filters, and hierarchies to interpret and act on complex data relationships. This empowers organizations to evolve from rule-based automations to AI systems that operate independently with confidence in the underlying data.)
/E (What sets the Universal Semantic Layer apart is its unique ability to support agentic AI systems that act autonomously and make informed decisions based on governed, consistent, and reusable metrics. By building a foundation of rich semantics, this layer not only feeds agents clean and reliable data but also equips them with contextual business logic, dynamic filters, and hierarchies to interpret and act on complex data relationships. This empowers organizations to evolve from rule-based automations to AI systems that operate independently with confidence in the underlying data.)
/Pg 14 0 R
>>
endobj
