304 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (This "neutral layer" approach, recommended by industry analysts, centralizes the cataloging of analytics content and metrics definitions, ensuring consistency across all tools. By simplifying access to structured, AI-ready data, users gain the flexibility to collaborate with both traditional analytics platforms and machine-learning models. When users or AI systems access data through this semantic layer, they interact with intuitive business objects like Customer or Revenue, rather than complex database tables. These definitions remain consistent whether in an executive dashboard, a departmental analysis, or an AI agent.)
/E (This "neutral layer" approach, recommended by industry analysts, centralizes the cataloging of analytics content and metrics definitions, ensuring consistency across all tools. By simplifying access to structured, AI-ready data, users gain the flexibility to collaborate with both traditional analytics platforms and machine-learning models. When users or AI systems access data through this semantic layer, they interact with intuitive business objects like Customer or Revenue, rather than complex database tables. These definitions remain consistent whether in an executive dashboard, a departmental analysis, or an AI agent.)
/Pg 15 0 R
>>
endobj
305 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Beyond providing consistent definitions, a robust semantic layer enables centralized security and permissions management, integrates data from multiple sources, and ensures compatibility with various BI tools through standard protocols. This decoupling of business logic from specific tools ensures crucial future-proofing, enabling organizations to migrate between data platforms, adapt emerging AI solutions, or consolidate analytics tools without rebuilding their entire semantic foundation.)
/E (Beyond providing consistent definitions, a robust semantic layer enables centralized security and permissions management, integrates data from multiple sources, and ensures compatibility with various BI tools through standard protocols. This decoupling of business logic from specific tools ensures crucial future-proofing, enabling organizations to migrate between data platforms, adapt emerging AI solutions, or consolidate analytics tools without rebuilding their entire semantic foundation.)
/Pg 15 0 R
>>
endobj
